    "summary": "Virginia ’82 delivers blazing High Time, Space‑Aiko and a monster Supplication",
    "review": "The night of September 14 1982 at the University of Virginia turned into one of those classic fall shows that still feels fresh when you press play. The band kicks off with a tight first set – Jack Straw rolls into Peggy‑O, then a raucous turn through El Paso and Bird Song before slipping into the lightning‑fast Lazy Lightning → Supplication → Deal sequence that sets the tone for the whole evening. Set two is where the magic really unfolds: a sparkling China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segues straight into Samson & Delilah, then High Time erupts with Jerry’s sweet, soaring vocals and Phil’s “bomb‑like” bass. The Estimated Prophet → He’s Gone stretch blossoms into a crisp drum duet, followed by a Space that blooms into an iconic Aiko jam, all under Brent’s shimmering keys. The second‑set marathon of Drums > Space > Iko Iko > Truckin' > Black Peter > I Need a Miracle > Bertha finishes on a high note, and the encore Johnny B. Goode leaves the crowd buzzing.",
